# RegForge — ENV TEMPLATE
# Is file ko .env.local me copy karo local dev ke liye.
# Vercel pe deploy karte time Vercel Dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables me
# inhi naam (Keys) ko add karo aur bas Value daal do — naam pehle se set hone chahiye.

# ===================== EASIEST: ONE VARIABLE =====================
# Vercel me sirf ek variable bana: Key = FIREBASE_CONFIG, Value = Firebase ka config snippet
# (apiKey: "...", authDomain: "...", projectId: "...", ...) as-is paste kar. Bas.
# Local me bhi chalega (single line):
FIREBASE_CONFIG=

# ===================== OR: INDIVIDUAL VARIABLES (optional) =====================
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix ke saath ya bina (FIREBASE_API_KEY) — dono chalte hain.
# Firebase Console → Project Settings → Your apps → Web app → Config se copy karo
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
# Optional - Analytics ke liye
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ===================== NOTES =====================
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix zaroori hai (Next.js client side ke liye)
# - Vercel pe har env ko Production, Preview, Development teeno me add karo
# - Without Firebase keys, admin sign-in is disabled; localStorage is only a fallback for questionnaire data
